Repository licensing scope

The repository owner authorized MIT licensing of researcher-original code on
21 November 2026. The MIT grant applies only to the source-file paths and
SHA-256 versions enumerated in MIT_LICENSED_FILES.csv. The unmodified MIT
license text and copyright notice are in LICENSES/MIT.txt.

This is not a blanket relicense of the repository or release attachments.
The copied upstream anomalib implementation retains its Intel copyright and
Apache-2.0 SPDX notice. Its applicable license text is included in
LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for provenance and path.

Dataset images and masks, auxiliary images, teacher weights, checkpoints,
ONNX/TensorRT engines, numerical arrays, experimental results, raw archives,
third-party dependencies and documents not listed in MIT_LICENSED_FILES.csv
are outside this original-code MIT grant. Their terms are not changed here.
No permission to redistribute excluded external assets is inferred.

Source bytes were not modified to add headers, preserving their evidence
hashes. Distribute the applicable license and scope information with the code.
